import 'dart:convert';

/// A tiny (64x64, 15s, ~8KB) real H.264/AAC MP4, embedded as a constant,
/// and a genuinely decodable video so `player.surface` scenarios (Fase 11)
/// exercise a real player rather than an opaque byte blob. Fixed content in,
/// fixed bytes out: the same run of the command below always produces this
/// exact file, which is what "deterministic bytes" means for
/// GET /stream/{version_id}, not that it's regenerated per request.
///
/// Fifteen seconds rather than the two it used to be (VER7): the player
/// scenarios pause first, and a pause that landed after the clip had ended
/// made them flaky. Not longer, because `tvos.home.hero-return-after-playback`
/// waits for the clip to end on its own, within 30 seconds. The audio is
/// silence, which keeps the AAC track small.
///
/// Regenerate with (ffmpeg 9.x, libx264/aac):
/// ```
/// ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i "color=c=0x2b6cb0:s=64x64:d=15:r=8" \\
///   -f lavfi -i "anullsrc=r=22050:cl=mono" -t 15 \\
///   -c:v libx264 -preset veryslow -crf 32 -pix_fmt yuv420p \\
///   -profile:v baseline -level 3.0 -c:a aac -b:a 24k -ar 22050 -ac 1 \\
///   -movflags +faststart sample_media.mp4
/// base64 -i sample_media.mp4
/// ```
const String sampleMediaMp4Base64 =
    '';

final List<int> sampleMediaMp4Bytes = base64Decode(sampleMediaMp4Base64);
